                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Left untreated, bacterial infections can be deadly, and effective treatment is becoming more challenging as bacteria becomes resistant to our most potent anti-bacterial drugs. That's why I am thankful for the continued work of @VenatorxPharma, a Malvern-based pharmaceutical research company, creating new anti-infectives to treat drug-resistant bacterial infections. Venatorx relies heavily on financial support from the National Institutes of Health (NIH), which President Trump has repeatedly attacked. \n\nThe Trump Administration has attempted to freeze NIH grants, reduce the cap on \"indirect\" research costs, and steeply cut the NIH's workforce. These moves won't just halt life-saving research; they are flat-out illegal. That is why I led a letter with my colleagues to the NIH director demanding a reversal of the unlawful change to the cap on indirect costs, and I am happy that a federal court has temporarily blocked the Trump Administration's harmful action, allowing vital biomedical research like that of Venatorx to continue.",
